All credit for the dashboard design, the rpcd backend architecture (cache,
bounded staleness, history, background poller) and the LuCI views belongs to
the original authors. This fork adapts that work to a different device; it is
not affiliated with or endorsed by them or by TP-Link.

Changes made in this fork (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)):
  - Data source: the G7's public ubus status over HTTP (xpon.public status and
    omci.agent status, one batched JSON-RPC request) instead of a telnet CLI.
    Only the address is required; a username and password are optional.
  - New awk parser (parse.awk): nW/m°C/µV/µA to dBm/°C/V/mA, GPON state O1-O7,
    ONU-ID, OLT profile, LOS from the module's own low-power alarm; the Rx/Tx
    warning and alarm limits come from the module (optical_class_source "module").
  - Output keeps the luci-app-vsol-ddm / -hsgq-ddm cache format, so the same
    dashboard and other consumers (e.g. Home NOC) read it unchanged.
  - Optional login (the G7's rpcd session): adds system information, the OMCI
    tables (MIB objects decoded in g7_ddm/omci.js) and restart; without it the
    public status is used and the dashboard links to the G7's web interface.
  - Dashboard and settings labels for the G7; no dependency on nc or timeout.
  - Data-driven unit tests (parser, backend) and router integration tests.
